{"type":"Feature","properties":{"kind":"port_limits","cargo":[],"osm":["way/1004233257","relation/15401088"],"source":"Derived: the convex hull of this port's terminals from OpenStreetMap, grown by 200 m, then cut to the water OpenStreetMap maps inside it (the sea within its coastline, rivers, docks and basins), with the terminals kept whole","licence":"ODbL-1.0","reviewed_at":"2026-11-23","clip":"water","note":"OpenStreetMap maps no port limits for Singapore. These are the hull of Tuas Port and Pasir Panjang Container Terminal, grown by 200 m and cut to the sea OpenStreetMap maps inside it, with the terminals kept whole: the terminals and the water between them, round Jurong Island and south of it, not the anchorages further out in the Strait. Jurong Island, the Tuas industrial estate and the Pasir Panjang shore are land and left out. A scan of OpenStreetMap finds no homes, residential land, schools, hospitals or places of worship inside. Sultan Shoal, a lighthouse islet, is inside, and the shore edge of Jurong Island reaches in by about 8 ha. The named places are the labels of Tuas View Extension, in a basin of Tuas Port, and of the Western Islands, in the water, a \"Port\" label on Pasir Panjang Terminal, and the planning-area outlines of Tuas and the Western Islands.","inside":{"houses":0,"residential_m2":0,"amenities":0,"places":[{"name":"Port","place":"neighbourhood","osm":"node/13348031207"},{"name":"Tuas View Extension","place":"neighbourhood","osm":"node/1830761721"},{"name":"Western Islands","place":"suburb","osm":"node/8804782085"}]}},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[103.614742,1.217486],[103.614478,1.217554],[103.614474,1.217276],[103.612942,1.217671],[103.613081,1.216519],[103.613471,1.215935],[103.614055,1.215545],[103.641557,1.20847],[103.642245,1.208333],[103.643985,1.208756],[103.786156,1.25334],[103.78674,1.25373],[103.78713,1.254314],[103.79624,1.269675],[103.795534,1.270069],[103.795609,1.270198],[103.795385,1.270331],[103.795322,1.2